---
import Page from '../../../components/Page.astro';
import { documents } from '../../../lib/data.js';
---
<Page title="Educators & Leaders" section="fund" image="/images/banner-educators.svg" alt="Illustration of a teacher and students in a classroom">
  <blockquote class="pull">
    <p>Of all the things a school controls, nothing shapes how much a child learns more than the teacher at the front of the room and the principal down the hall.</p>
    <footer>&mdash; <a href="/uploads/2025/08/Wexmoor-Foundation-Impact-Plan-rev-8.2025.pdf">The Wexmoor Foundation Impact Plan</a></footer>
  </blockquote>
  <p>Research consistently finds that teachers are the most important in-school influence on student achievement, and that school leaders play a critical role as well, especially in keeping excellent teachers. Principals create the conditions in which great teaching and learning can happen.</p>
  <p>Our goal is to invest in high-performing, results-focused, sustainable programs and strategies that advance these goals for teachers and leaders:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Recruiting the most qualified candidates into the profession</li>
    <li>Developing current educators so they can better help students achieve</li>
    <li>Retaining the most effective educators</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Outcomes Sought</h3>
  <p>We support organizations that measure their results and use evidence-based strategies. Ultimately, we want to see growth in student achievement as a result of excellent teachers and leaders. Building on our priorities of recruiting, developing and retaining educators, we place particular emphasis on one outcome: effective teachers remaining in their schools for at least three years. Our <a href={documents.outcomes.path}>Outcomes Sought document</a> summarizes our priorities and serves as a basis for conversation with grantees.</p>
  <hr />
  <h1 class="section-title">Strategic Issue: Strong Teachers for Every Classroom</h1>
  <figure class="centered-figure">
    <img src="/images/educators-issue.svg" alt="Illustration of a teacher at the board with students" width="600" height="338" />
  </figure>
  <p>Teachers are the most important school-based factor in a student&rsquo;s academic success. There are outstanding teachers in every North Carolina district. Yet students from low-income families and students of color are less likely to be taught by the most effective teachers, whether across schools or within them.</p>
  <p>Our goal is simple: increase the likelihood that every student is taught by a highly effective teacher.</p>
  <hr />
  <h3>Strategies</h3>
  <p>The Wexmoor Foundation is committed to finding and advancing ways to grow the pool of well-prepared new teachers and to multiply the reach of highly effective teachers.</p>
  <div class="image-cards">
    <div>
      <h3>Grow the Pipeline</h3>
      <img src="/images/grow-pipeline.svg" alt="Illustration of a student teacher with a mentor teacher" width="600" height="400" />
      <p>Growing the pool of effective new teachers by:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Strengthening clinical experiences, including residencies, for teacher candidates who are likely to be hired into and succeed in high-poverty schools</li>
        <li>Building shared ownership between school districts and educator preparation programs</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Multiply the Reach</h3>
      <img src="/images/multiply-reach.svg" alt="Illustration of a teacher leading a small team" width="600" height="400" />
      <p>Multiplying the reach of highly effective teachers so that principals are:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Using effectiveness data to match teachers with the students who need the most support</li>
        <li>Adopting staffing models in which excellent teachers lead small teams and reach more students</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="button-row">
    <a class="btn-outline" href={documents.logicModel.path}>Explore the Logic Model</a>
    <a class="btn-outline" href={documents.impactPlan.path}>Explore the Full Strategy and Impact Plan</a>
  </div>
  <hr />
  <h3>Additional Information</h3>
  <p>The Foundation dedicates time and advocacy, its work beyond grantmaking, to this strategic issue. Our two grantmaking focus areas, <a href="/what-we-fund/early-grades-achievement/">Early Grades Achievement</a> and Educators &amp; Leaders, adopted by the Board in 2014, remain unchanged. Read Brannock, launched with Foundation support in 2016, and early reading proficiency remain a top priority and strategic issue for the Foundation.</p>
  <hr />
  <h3>Data That Inspires Our Approach</h3>
  <p><strong>Why we need to grow the pipeline</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>Brannock County Schools employs roughly 2,100 classroom teachers. Each year, about one in six classrooms in the district&rsquo;s highest-poverty schools is led by a teacher in their first three years.</li>
    <li>Beginning teachers are more likely to be hired late in the summer and placed in higher-poverty schools, where turnover is also highest.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><strong>Why we need to multiply the reach</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>When excellent teachers lead small teams of colleagues, more students experience top-quartile instruction.</li>
    <li>In Brannock County Schools, 41% of students in low-poverty schools were taught by a teacher who exceeded expected growth the prior year, compared with 24% of students in high-poverty schools.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><img src="/images/data-chart.svg" alt="Bar chart: 41% of students in low-poverty schools versus 24% in high-poverty schools were taught by a teacher who exceeded expected growth" width="600" height="464" /></p>
</Page>
